/P 868 0 R
/E (An autoencoder is a type of artificial neural network used for unsupervised learning. It is designed to encode the input data into a lower-dimensional representation and then decode it back to the original data. The primary objective is to learn an efficient and compressed representation of the input data.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
349 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 869 0 R
/E (The basic structure of an autoencoder consists of two main components:)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
